source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: A backslash does not protect the parameter separator: Jira titles the panel `a` and reads the rest as another parameter, which JFM cannot express.
-- input.jira --
{panel:title=a\|b}
text
{panel}
-- rendered.html --
<div class="panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="panelHeader" style="border-bottom-width: 1px;"><b>a</b></div><div class="panelContent">
<p>text</p>
</div></div>
-- want.md --
{panel:title=a\\|b}
text
{panel}
-- warnings.json --
[
 {
  "Line": 1,
  "Column": 17,
  "Construct": "directive",
  "Reason": "unknown panel attribute is preserved"
 },
 {
  "Line": 1,
  "Column": 17,
  "Construct": "jira-macro",
  "Reason": "Jira parameter without a value cannot be represented by this JFM attribute; complete panel remains literal"
 }
]
